      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'd like to add that the state the avatar is in only seems to be reset locally, so other clients will still see the avatar in the previous state. So even if it's decided to continue resetting the states when Calibrate is pressed, at least make it so it gets reset across remote clients as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-16T03:43:42.885Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, FBT recalibration results in resetting your avatar. This can be inconvenient if you've set up a bunch of persistent states. Recalibration should just force the pose to T-pose and then calibrate with the current avatar state; if resetting the avatar is actually desired, there's already a separate option for that.",
